1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:01,982
In this town, everybody boings.

2
00:00:02,012 --> 00:00:02,739
Except me.

3
00:00:03,039 --> 00:00:05,697
Okay. I used to boing the highest.

4
00:00:05,667 --> 00:00:09,331
Over the fence. Over the mailman. Every single morning.

5
00:00:09,481 --> 00:00:12,266
Then one day, my boing was just... gone.

6
00:00:12,516 --> 00:00:14,467
The doctor tapped my knee. Nothing.

7
00:00:14,467 --> 00:00:17,047
Too much boinging. No boinging for a month.

8
00:00:17,197 --> 00:00:20,008
The Sky Race was in one week, so I tried everything.

9
00:00:20,058 --> 00:00:21,768
Nine sodas. I just burped.

10
00:00:21,768 --> 00:00:24,155
Springs on my shoes. I got stuck to the ceiling.

11
00:00:24,155 --> 00:00:26,734
Grandma's trampoline. It launched me into the mailbox.

12
00:00:26,834 --> 00:00:28,809
Even my cat boings better than me now.

13
00:00:29,059 --> 00:00:31,119
Then my best friend yelled from her roof.

14
00:00:31,069 --> 00:00:34,357
Rooftop party tonight! Oh wait, you can't get up here anyway.

15
00:00:34,457 --> 00:00:35,738
I shut the window.

16
00:00:36,038 --> 00:00:39,308
So while they danced on the roofs, I trained in the garage.

17
00:00:39,308 --> 00:00:42,460
No boing. Just me and gravity. Every single night.

18
00:00:42,560 --> 00:00:45,767
For the first time in years, the mailman finished his route.

19
00:00:46,067 --> 00:00:47,878
Then came the race.

20
00:00:47,928 --> 00:00:51,305
The other team boinged so high, they waved at airplanes.

21
00:00:51,255 --> 00:00:53,342
BOING! BOING! BOING!

22
00:00:53,442 --> 00:00:57,017
Ten seconds left. One giant gap. We were losing.

23
00:00:57,067 --> 00:00:59,370
I bent my knees. I pushed.

24
00:00:59,340 --> 00:01:02,688
Hnnng... almost... almost... almost... ALMOST!

25
00:01:02,738 --> 00:01:04,352
The other team started laughing.

26
00:01:04,502 --> 00:01:07,970
Five seconds. Seven nights of squats, all saved up.

27
00:01:08,020 --> 00:01:09,571
And then... it came back.

28
00:01:09,671 --> 00:01:10,208
BOING!

29
00:01:10,308 --> 00:01:13,343
I flew so high, I high-fived a bird.

30
00:01:13,343 --> 00:01:18,171
I landed on the finish line. The scoreboard fell over. The ref's hat flew into the next town.

31
00:01:18,221 --> 00:01:19,130
We won!

32
00:01:19,430 --> 00:01:22,184
That night, the whole town was boinging again.

33
00:01:22,284 --> 00:01:23,367
Except the ref.

34
00:01:23,467 --> 00:01:25,330
He's still looking for his hat.

